{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.409,
   "text": "My dad kept a box of road flares in my trunk... and one rule, taped inside the lid."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.009,
   "end": 14.831,
   "text": "If you break down at night, light one flare behind the car. Just one."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.431,
   "end": 20.7,
   "text": "And if you ever see a second flare down the road... lock the doors. Don't wave for help."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.6,
   "end": 27.04,
   "text": "Last winter, my car died on an empty mountain road, an hour past midnight."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.64,
   "end": 33.677,
   "text": "I lit one flare, set it behind the bumper, and climbed back inside to wait for the tow truck."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 34.277,
   "end": 39.269,
   "text": "For twenty minutes... nothing. Just snow, and that red light hissing in the mirror."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 40.269,
   "end": 44.557,
   "text": "Then, far down the road behind me... a second flare lit up."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 46.757,
   "end": 49.531,
   "text": "I locked the doors. I didn't wave."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.731,
   "end": 54.144,
   "text": "A minute later, a third flare lit. Closer."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 55.544,
   "end": 61.048,
   "text": "Then a fourth. Close enough to see the snow falling around it... and nobody standing there."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 62.448,
   "end": 65.456,
   "text": "Then, one by one... they all went out."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 67.856,
   "end": 72.976,
   "text": "When the tow truck finally came, the driver found me curled up on the back seat."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 73.576,
   "end": 79.677,
   "text": "He walked around with his flashlight, opened my trunk... and asked why my flare box was empty."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 81.077,
   "end": 84.512,
   "text": "Dad always packs six. I'd only taken one."
  }
 ],
